# Example 04: Scatter Scout

## Tool Fan-out Surface

Scatter Scout is The Archivist's multi-source search fan-out. One visitor question becomes a set of JSON-serializable tool worksets: OpenLibrary keyword search, Google Books, OpenLibrary subject search, Wikipedia enrichment, or whichever registered tool DAGs the plan selects.

The parent DAG still asks for one ranked answer. Scatter exists here because each source can run independently, report its own outcome, and return candidates in a deterministic shape that downstream ranking can trust.

## Scout Flow and Container Path

### DAG registration and diagram

