# Example 14: Gather Strategies

## Gather Strategy Surface

Gather Strategies decide how producer results become parent state. The Cartographer uses them as runtime logic: the top-level `fold-insights` gather folds stream records into bounded aggregates, and the `geo-weighted-fusion` gather fuses embedded geo resolver outputs into a selected location.

The focus here is merge policy, not fan-out. Scatter runs clone work; first-class gather placements decide what the parent sees after each clone, after the whole scatter, or at an explicit graph-visible barrier.

## Cartographer Gather Flows

### DAG registration and diagram

The [Cartographer](./the-cartographer) runtime exercises the real gather examples. Its top-level `process-stream` scatter routes to `fold-insights`, which uses `insights-fold` to update bounded insight state; its `geo-source-resolve` sub-DAG makes fusion graph-visible with a first-class `geo-weighted-fusion` gather node.

